## 🚀 Quick start

```bash
cp .env.sample .env            # defaults are fine to start with
uv sync                        # creates .venv/ AND uv.lock

make run_pipeline              # preprocess -> train -> evaluate -> predict
make run_local_api             # the API starts on http://127.0.0.1:8000
```

Commit the `uv.lock` that `uv sync` just generated: the CI installs with
`uv sync --frozen`, which fails without it, and so
does the `Dockerfile`.

`make run_pipeline` works with **no cloud account at all**: the project ships with a
synthetic dataset, trains a reference scikit-learn model and produces
predictions. Replace the pieces one at a time with your own afterwards (see
[Adapting this project](#-adapting-this-project)).

